message.content:
Write a concrete EXECUTION PLAN for "Compressed Air Leak Detection" built around the RED-TEAMED reality (not the optimistic pitch). Founder: Hooman ($25-150K; ~10-20 hrs/wk; wants $5-30K/mo; NOT his domain). Red-team findings (JSON): {
  "name": "Compressed Air Leak Detection",
  "slug": "compressed_air_leaks",
  "assumptions_checked": [
    {
      "claim": "Only UE Systems overlaps; no purpose-built continuous compressed-air leak monitoring for the mid-market",
      "status": "FALSE",
      "evidence": "Atlas Copco SMARTAIRNET+SMARTLINK ship a wireless point-of-use IIoT sensor network marketed to 'reveal leaks/anomalies/energy losses'; Kaeser KMT sensor suite + ADA audits; UE OnTrak+950BT wireless; CS Instruments LD500 + 30-MEMS ultrasound camera; Sonotec compressed-air leak management line; Prosaris OL2 + cloud Platform; Fluke ii900/ii910; SDT; Distran. Mature crowded category, not an empty lane (vendor materials, 2026-07-02)."
    },
    {
      "claim": "Compressor OEMs monitor supply side only, can't localize demand-side leaks (complementary not competitive)",
      "status": "FALSE",
      "evidence": "Atlas Copco SMARTAIRNET explicitly extends to 'point of use' to fill the generation-to-consumption 'blind spot' and reveal leaks; Kaeser KMT is a point-of-use sensor suite. OEMs already ship demand-side wireless leak analytics into accounts they own."
    },
    {
      "claim": "~$1,600 to a working prototype (implied as venture cost)",
      "status": "PARTIALLY-TRUE",
      "evidence": "$1.6K = breadboard PoC only; doc's own table shows $8K pilot, $15K launch, and omits FCC/CE cert (~$10-30K/SKU), enclosure tooling, FTO legal ($5K), and inventory. Real sellable-product capital $50-150K."
    },
    {
      "claim": "Irrefutable ROI: leaks waste 20-30% of compressed-air energy",
      "status": "VERIFIED",
      "evidence": "DOE/Compressed Air Challenge figure is real — but it cuts against the startup: it's why utilities (Avista, Consumers Energy) and compressor dealers already provide leak audits FREE, undermining paid WTP."
    },
    {
      "claim": "Universal market, SAM $500M+",
      "status": "PARTIALLY-TRUE",
      "evidence": "Whole leak-detection market ~$1.2-3B, 7-9% CAGR (DataIntelo/QY/MarketIntelo), but dominated by incumbents+handheld HW; TAM-not-SAM trap. Addressable slice for an unknown solo HW founder vs free audits + OEM bundling is tiny."
    },
    {
      "claim": "ML $/month-per-leak severity is the differentiator / data moat",
      "status": "FALSE",
      "evidence": "CS Instruments LD500 already auto-computes leak flow + cost-per-year-per-leak and prints audit reports with no ML — a table-stakes feature of a $3-5K handheld."
    },
    {
      "claim": "Fluke acoustic imager ~$10-15K",
      "status": "FALSE",
      "evidence": "Fluke ii900 street price ≈ $25,427 (ValueTesters, 2026-07-02); premium category, understated in doc."
    },
    {
      "claim": "Recurring $200/mo SaaS, self-serve land-and-expand, minimal marginal cost",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "evidence": "No WTP validation for perpetual monitoring; value is front-loaded (leaks found once), plants historically buy periodic surveys; hardware has RMA/battery/support marginal cost. High churn risk."
    },
    {
      "claim": "Founder-market fit 7/10",
      "status": "FALSE",
      "evidence": "Success axes are PCB/STM32/RF/enclosure/FCC-cert/contract-mfg/inventory (a hardware company, not his domain) plus industrial maintenance-manager relationships (his weakness); ML/cloud layer is the commoditized part. Inverted fit, ~3-4."
    }
  ],
  "competitors": [
    "Atlas Copco SMARTAIRNET + SMARTLINK — wireless point-of-use IIoT sensor network with leak/anomaly detection, sold by the #1 compressor OEM into accounts it already owns (near-zero CAC)",
    "Kaeser — Air Demand Analysis audits + Kaeser Measurement Technology (KMT) intelligent sensor suite + ultrasonic detectors with onboard leak-cost calc",
    "UE Systems — OnTrak continuous wireless monitoring + 950BT sensor; 50+ yr category leader (est. $20-50M rev)",
    "Fluke (Teledyne) ii900/ii910 acoustic imagers — 124-mic cameras, ii900 ≈ $25.4K, global distribution",
    "CS Instruments — LD500/LD510 detectors that auto-calculate leak flow + cost/yr + audit report, plus 30-MEMS beam-forming ultrasound camera",
    "Sonotec — dedicated 'Leak Management of Compressed Air Systems' line (strong EU)",
    "Prosaris — OL2 handheld + cloud PROSARIS Platform (event records, facility data, compressor setups) = already a leak-management SaaS",
    "SDT International; Distran (SonicView acoustic imaging, customers incl. Shell/Air Liquide/NASA)",
    "Free substitutes: utility rebate audits (Avista acoustic-imaging leak program, Consumers Energy free consult + up to ~$10K rebate) and free compressor-dealer leak surveys (Evergreen Compressed Air, ALD, Energy Design Engineers)"
  ],
  "honest_economics": "Base case (most probable): $0/mo — stalls at the hardware/FCC-cert/field-reliability wall or loses every deal to a free utility/dealer audit and OEM-bundled analytics. ~10-15% upside: <$1-2K/mo net at 18-24 months (e.g. ~5 plants at $5K kit + $200/mo, with hardware margin eaten by RMA/support/field time), after $50-150K real capital — NOT the pitched $1.6K. Versus original claim of universal market + irrefutable ROI + recurring SaaS. Gross ($200/mo × N + $5K kit) is not net; kit is mostly COGS/support.",
  "hrs_per_week": "12-20 hrs/wk, non-delegable, mixing firmware/RF debugging, field installs, RMA logistics, and industrial cold sales — the least AI-safe, least delegable load in the candidate set; directly competes with (and is worse than) CutLog's build hours",
  "kill_risks": [
    "OEM bundling: Atlas Copco SMARTAIRNET / Kaeser KMT deliver wireless demand-side leak analytics from the vendor already in the compressor room at near-zero CAC — uncontestable distribution",
    "Free substitute: utility rebate audits + free compressor-dealer leak surveys already give the buyer the headline ROI for $0",
    "Hardware/cert/inventory wall outside founder's domain (PCB/RF/FCC-CE/enclosure/RMA) at 10-20 hrs/wk solo — most likely pre-revenue stall point",
    "Front-loaded value vs recurring price: leaks found once, high SaaS churn after first fix cycle; $200/mo stream unproven",
    "Commodity analytics: ML '$/month per leak' is already a stock feature of a $3-5K CS Instruments LD500 handheld — no moat"
  ],
  "revised_score": 3.6,
  "verdict": "PASS",
  "confidence": "HIGH",
  "_t": {
    "slug": "compressed_air",
    "name": "Compressed Air Leak Detection",
    "read": "/home/colligo/hs_scripts/claude/auto_research/deep_research/compressed_air_leaks/ (01-05 docs) and its row in /home/colligo/hs_scripts/claude/auto_research/deep_research/MASTER_COMPARISON.md (optimistic 7.65).",
    "claims": "HW+SW, ~$1.6K to validate, universal market (every factory has compressed air), irrefutable ROI (leaks waste 20-30% of compressed-air energy), only UE Systems overlaps. RED-TEAM SKEPTICALLY: ultrasonic leak detection is a mature category — who ALREADY sells this (UE Systems, Fluke ii900/ii910 acoustic imagers, SDT, Prosaris, CS Instruments, Sonotec, Distran)? Are compressor OEMs (Atlas Copco, Ingersoll Rand, Kaeser SmartLink) bundling leak analytics? Is the buyer a plant that already hires energy auditors / gets utility-rebate audits for free? Is WTP real or is this a one-time $400 handheld + a free utility audit? Gross vs net, realistic ramp, honest hrs/wk."
  }
}
Also read /home/colligo/hs_scripts/claude/auto_research/runs/trackA_redteam/compressed_air/01_redteam.md.

If the red-team verdict is PASS, still write the plan BUT lead with the honest "why this is likely not worth it" and what would have to be true to change that. Plan must cover: the specific target segment/wedge, first 90 days week-by-week, path to revenue + realistic ramp, itemized budget within $25-150K, delegation to keep it part-time, go/no-go gates, and cheapest validation before spending real money.
WRITE to /home/colligo/hs_scripts/claude/auto_research/runs/trackA_redteam/compressed_air/02_execution_plan.md (use Write). Return a ~180-word summary and pass along the slug.
